In real case I need get some queue of matches, from lists (groups) of participants. That in first match play all first participants from different groups. In second match play all second participants and so on. And I will not be able to sort it out. If you want just to combine the lists without altering their order, then you can do something like:


    public static void main(String[] args) {
    List one = Arrays.asList("one","four","seven");
    List two = Arrays.asList("two","five","eight");
    List three = Arrays.asList("three","six");
    System.out.println(zipLists(one, two, three)); 
    //[one, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight]
    }
    public static List zipLists(List... lists) {
    int maxSize = 0, totalSize = 0;
    List> iterators = new ArrayList<>(lists.length);
    for(List list: lists) {
    int size = list.size();
    maxSize = Math.max(maxSize, size);
    totalSize += size;
    iterators.add(list.iterator());
    }
    List mergedList = new ArrayList<>(totalSize);
    for(int i = 0; i < maxSize; i++) {
    for(Iterator iterator: iterators) {
    if(iterator.hasNext()) {
    mergedList.add(iterator.next());
    }
    }
    }
    return mergedList;
    }

